bug_report:
Bug opaque type fields are visible outside implementation module
As reported on the gm2 mailing list:

Opaque type fields are visible outside the implementation module.  Consider:

$ cat MinOpaque.def

DEFINITION MODULE MinOpaque;
TYPE Opaque;
PROCEDURE Make (VAR o: Opaque; i: INTEGER);
END MinOpaque.


$ cat MinOpaque.mod:
IMPLEMENTATION MODULE MinOpaque;
FROM Storage IMPORT ALLOCATE, DEALLOCATE;
FROM SYSTEM IMPORT TSIZE;

TYPE Opaque = POINTER TO INTEGER;

PROCEDURE Make (VAR o: Opaque; i: INTEGER);
BEGIN
     ALLOCATE (o, TSIZE (Opaque));
     o^ := i;
END Make;

END MinOpaque.

$ cat TryMinOpaque.mod

MODULE TryMinOpaque;
FROM InOut IMPORT WriteString, WriteLn, WriteInt;
FROM MinOpaque IMPORT Opaque, Make;

VAR o: Opaque;

BEGIN
     Make (o, 10);
     o^ := 20;                  (* I thought this was illegal. *)
     WriteString ("o^: "); WriteInt (o^, 0); WriteLn;
END TryMinOpaque.


The compiler should forbid access to the internals of the Opaque type.

